-- title:
--   The top procedure of the filtering host at σ = 0.0336175 writes the all-edges flags
-- statement:
--   Let procedure $p_O$ of $P_0$ solve `Light.Filter2.oracleTask` with time $T_o$ and need $\nu_o$, and let the parameter procedures (`ParamProcs`), the sieve, prime-filter and fill procedures (`TopProcs`), the core and round bodies, the procedures of a round (`RoundProcs`) and of the final answer (`FinalProcs`) be in place in $P_0\mathbin{+\!\!+}R$. If `Env` holds for the all-edges instance $x$ at depth $d$ with first memory $\mu_0$ and free pointer $f$, then `topBody`, run in the frame $[n,U,ab,bc,ac,out,f]$, ends within `tTop To n U` steps with the all-edges flags `aeFlags n AB BC AC` at `x.out` and every other cell below $f$ as in $\mu_0$.
